{
  "sn24.8:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.8 ",
  "sn24.8:0.2": "1. Stream-Entry ",
  "sn24.8:0.3": "The Extensive View ",
  "sn24.8:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.8:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.8:1.3": "‘There are these seven substances that are not made, not derived, not created, without a creator, barren, steady as a mountain peak, standing firm like a pillar. ",
  "sn24.8:1.4": "They don’t move or deteriorate or obstruct each other. They’re unable to cause pleasure, pain, or both pleasure and pain to each other. ",
  "sn24.8:1.5": "What seven? ",
  "sn24.8:1.6": "The substances of earth, water, fire, air; pleasure, pain, and the soul is the seventh. ",
  "sn24.8:1.7": "These seven substances are not made, not derived, not created, without a creator, barren, steady as a mountain peak, standing firm like a pillar. ",
  "sn24.8:1.8": "They don’t move or deteriorate or obstruct each other. They’re unable to cause pleasure, pain, or both pleasure and pain to each other. ",
  "sn24.8:1.9": "If you chop off someone’s head with a sharp sword, you don’t take anyone’s life. ",
  "sn24.8:1.10": "The sword simply passes through the gap between the seven substances. ",
  "sn24.8:1.11": "There are 1.4 million main wombs, and 6,000, and 600; 500 deeds, and five, and three; deeds and half-deeds; 62 paths of practice, 62 sub-eons, six classes of rebirth, and eight stages in a person’s life; 4,900 Ājīvaka ascetics, 4